{"results":[{"key":"consolidated/re-cinq-lore/1792560610823","value":"Ingest Age Advancement Is Tightly Scoped to Default-Branch Deltas — Facts 2-5 establish that only default-branch CI deltas cause the displayed ingest age to advance; all other activities (overlay deltas, 409s, intermediate chunks) do not. This is a critical boundary condition future agents must preserve in any changes to ingest-age logic or testing.","score":1,"agent_id":"consolidation","source":"memory","backend":"utopia"},{"key":"consolidated/re-cinq-re-plan/1792560606750","value":"CI validation acts as a gate for format compatibility — all CI checks passing on PR #300 combined with successful code review approval indicates the YAML restructuring was not only syntactically correct but also compatible with the entire build/test pipeline.","score":0.9855676238654961,"agent_id":"consolidation","source":"memory","backend":"utopia"},{"key":"consolidated/re-cinq-lore#2731/1792128610834","value":"Sequential dependency cycles between CI gates and output generation create deadlock conditions — mark-ready (which writes required PR sections) cannot run until CI passes, but CI validation checks for those same sections in the draft body. Future agents should decouple validation checks from sequential stage gates by either pre-validating section templates before CI, or deferring section requirement checks until after mark-ready execution.","score":0.9834662003604524,"agent_id":"consolidation","source":"memory","backend":"utopia"},{"key":"consolidated/re-cinq-lore#1911/1788931839082","value":"When reading external system state (CI verdicts, check runs), anchor reads to the newest authoritative commit signal rather than assuming all commits generate observable events — GitHub's behavior around format commits and skip-CI markers means you must filter for commits that actually triggered checks.","score":0.9802153606642449,"agent_id":"consolidation","source":"memory","backend":"utopia"},{"key":"consolidated/re-cinq-lore#1062/1786512635517","value":"Post-incident branch remediation is incomplete until history is force-purged and developers are notified to rebase — leaving malware payloads in commit history or allowing branches to persist on old main creates lingering risk, even after the main branch is fixed and workflows are hardened.","score":0.9605859783746076,"agent_id":"consolidation","source":"memory","backend":"utopia"},{"key":"consolidated/re-cinq-lore#1062/1786339808280","value":"Post-incident branch management requires explicit rebasing of all branches cut from compromised commits onto the fixed main branch, since malware payloads persist in branch histories even after main remediation — track and communicate this to developers rather than assuming branch cleanup is automatic.","score":0.9437689969604863,"agent_id":"consolidation","source":"memory","backend":"utopia"},{"key":"dod/otto-197-bounce-handling-blocked","value":"DoD triage for re-cinq/Otto#197 (Read escalation mail bounces instead of trusting relay acceptance) -> changes_requested (BLOCKED). RE-CONFIRMED 2026-09-21 (this is at least the 2nd dod run; prior acceptance-dod node erroneously reported outcome:success but pushed nothing -> "issue-197 has no changes against the default branch". success falsely validates an empty branch; correct outcome is changes_requested/Lore-Dod-Blocked with NO commit, same pattern as otto-154/otto-196).

