WHY BLOCKED (re-verified on filesystem this run):","score":0.8602463605823067,"agent_id":"1ead2924-7bd0-4d66-9e27-ad2d5bf8bffb","source":"memory","backend":"utopia"},{"key":"consolidated/re-cinq-lore#2731/1791869405741","value":"Circular dependency between output format and validation prevents agent progress — mark-ready (which fixes PR body format) requires green CI, but CI fails due to missing that format. Break such cycles by either generating compliant output earlier in the pipeline or by relaxing validation order; document which direction is chosen.","score":0.8291510567611508,"agent_id":"consolidation","source":"memory","backend":"utopia"},{"key":"consolidated/re-cinq-lore#1062/1786426212531","value":"Post-incident branches remain compromised until explicitly rebased onto the fixed main; inventory all branches cut before the fix commit and enforce rebase-before-merge policies, since malware payloads persist in branch history independently of the main remediation.","score":0.814232075809047,"agent_id":"consolidation","source":"memory","backend":"utopia"},{"key":"consolidated/re-cinq-lore#2071/1789882235563","value":"The acceptance-dod node's assumption that HEAD == origin/main blocks red-test creation — either relax this guard, add explicit logging when skipped, or pre-flight check branch freshness before entering the dod loop to surface conflicts earlier.","score":0.8109422492401215,"agent_id":"consolidation","source":"memory","backend":"utopia"}],"notes":[]}
